This Week:
    PATH PARAM
    (example from fake store api swagger:https://api.escuelajs.co/docs#/ /products endpoint and /products/{id} endpoints difference:
        -> Returns single set of data from list of resources
        -> It is part of URL
        -> /api/products/ --> returns all products
        -> /api/products/{id} --> returns single product
        -> /api/products/2 --> returns single product

    What is going on behind the scene?
    We are typing a query and sending it to get data:
        public static void getProduct(int id){

            SELECT * FROM PRODUCTS
            WHERE ID=id;

        }

    QUERY PARAM

            Book Name=Blindness
            Author=Jose Saramago

        -> It filters data based on K&V which is provided into API doc
        -> KEY and VALUE needs to be defined in API doc based on endpoints
        -> It is NOT part of URL and starts after ?
        -> /products
        ? -> End Of URL
        offset=0   --> K&V
        &
        limit=10   --> K&V


    VERIFY RESPONSES
        - Contains  --> not suggested
        - response.path()
        - jsonPath()

